What:		/sys/bus/usb/devices/<busnum>-<devnum>:<config num>.<interface num>/<hid-bus>:<vendor-id>:<product-id>.<num>/quirks
Date:		November 2011
Contact:	Benjamin Tissoires <benjamin.tissoires@gmail.com>
Description:	The integer value of this attribute corresponds to the
		quirks actually in place to handle the device's protocol.
		When read, this attribute returns the current settings (see
		MT_QUIRKS_* in hid-multitouch.c).
		When written this attribute change on the fly the quirks, then
		the protocol to handle the device.

What:		/sys/bus/{i2c,usb}/devices/.../<hid-bus>:<vendor-id>:<product-id>.<num>/click_force_level
Date:		April 2026
Contact:	linux-input@vger.kernel.org
Description:	Click activation force preference for haptic touchpads that
		expose a vendor-defined Digitizers usage 0xB0 feature in
		grams. Reading returns the currently configured discrete
		level. Writing a value within
		[click_force_level_min, click_force_level_max] (commonly
		1..3, mapping to firmware-specific gram thresholds) applies
		the new preference and persists it across runtime
		suspend/resume. This attribute is only present on devices
		that expose the corresponding HID feature.

What:		/sys/bus/{i2c,usb}/devices/.../<hid-bus>:<vendor-id>:<product-id>.<num>/click_force_level_min
What:		/sys/bus/{i2c,usb}/devices/.../<hid-bus>:<vendor-id>:<product-id>.<num>/click_force_level_max
Date:		April 2026
Contact:	linux-input@vger.kernel.org
Description:	Inclusive bounds of valid values that may be written to
		click_force_level on this device. Read-only, fixed for the
		lifetime of the device. Allows userspace to size a slider
		without probing-and-checking errno.

What:		/sys/bus/{i2c,usb}/devices/.../<hid-bus>:<vendor-id>:<product-id>.<num>/haptic_intensity
Date:		April 2026
Contact:	linux-input@vger.kernel.org
Description:	Haptic actuator intensity preference (typically 0..100,
		percent) for haptic touchpads that expose a standalone HID
		Simple Haptic Controller Intensity feature - i.e. the
		firmware autonomously generates click/release waveforms and
		only accepts a strength preference. Writes are clamped to
		[haptic_intensity_min, haptic_intensity_max]. Devices that
		implement the full HID Haptic protocol with
		AutoTrigger/ManualTrigger expose intensity as a per-effect
		parameter via the FF_HAPTIC evdev API instead, and do not
		present this attribute.

What:		/sys/bus/{i2c,usb}/devices/.../<hid-bus>:<vendor-id>:<product-id>.<num>/haptic_intensity_min
What:		/sys/bus/{i2c,usb}/devices/.../<hid-bus>:<vendor-id>:<product-id>.<num>/haptic_intensity_max
Date:		April 2026
Contact:	linux-input@vger.kernel.org
Description:	Inclusive bounds of valid values that may be written to
		haptic_intensity on this device. Read-only, fixed for the
		lifetime of the device.
